Time for the RD-53 words of Lazarus again I think...

If you really need to get the data off an RD-53 that has its heads
stuck, here is how to have a good chance of doing it.

Undo the electronic board, and swing it out. You will see a 2 way
connector that goes to the EMA coil. Remove it.

Put the drive in a plastic bag, and seal it. Place in freezer
overnight. Yes, `freeze' the sucker...

Remove the drive, connect it, and power up. Let it come to full
speed and wait 10 sec or so. Plug the EMA back in. With luck,
the heads will now load and you can copy the data off.

