> 
> Local> Show Telnet Listener 2020
> 
> Listener TCP-port:  2020                     Listener Type:  TELNET 
> Identification:     Important_Device
> Ports:              20
> Connections:        Enabled 
> IP Address:         1.2.3.4
> 
> 
> 	Anyone know if it is possible to get the simple security working here?
> 
> Thanks!
> Rick

Rick,

I can confirm this when I telnet to a specific port with the telnet
listener enabled on it.  When the remote password is enabled, you
still get the "#" prompt prior to be "connected through."  In other
words, it uses the same prompt as when you telnet to the server (i.e.
1.2.3.4) without specifying a port.

Try the following:

CHANGE PORT 2020 REMOTE PASSWORD ENABLE
LOGOUT PORT 2020

You should then see the "Remote Password" characteristic enabled when
you do a "SHOW PORT 20"

Then try "telnet 1.2.3.4 2020" and see if you get the "#" prompt.  If
you do, type the remote password for the server (it will be access if
you didn't change it).  Hit return a couple of times after entering
the password at the "#" prompt.

Joel


