Bob Willard wrote:

> Eric Smith wrote:
> >
> > I wrote:
> > > Speaking of which, I just bought two CIPCA-AA at auction and would like
> > > to write a Linux driver.  Was any programming information on the CIPCA
> > > published?  If not, is there any way to get the source to the
> > > SYS$PCA without spending a vast amount of money?
> >
> > "Kenneth H. Fairfield" <Kenneth.H.Fairfield@spam-be-gone.intel.com.net> writes:
> > > Before you get too far along with this, are you aware that the
> > > HSC50 is NOT supported by CIPCA's?  That is, you must REMOVE
> > > any HSC50s on the CI if you're going to have any CIPCA's on
> > > it.
> >
> > Sounds like it's just a software issue, especially since it does work with
> > the HSC70.  Doesn't the HSC70  uses the same CI interface module (L0100)
> > as the HSC50?
> >
> > Anyhow, I won't be connecting an HSC50 to the CIPCA.  The CIPCA will be
> > connected to a CI20 on a KL10, and I want to write Linux software
> > (including a CIPCA driver) to simulate an HSC50 in 576-byte-block mode
> > for use with TOPS-10.
>
> I think you are hosed.  IIRC, the CIPCA (both -AA and -BA versions)
> can only share a CI with other nodes that support 4K packets; that's
> why HSC50s and older CI host adapters are disallowed.  {ISTR that some
> HSC70s and/or some CIXCDs/CIBCAs had to be brought up to rev for 4K
> packets, but I won't swear to that.}  The CIPCA was never tried with
> a CI20, and I'll give good odds that CI20s don't use 4K packets.

The problem with the HSC50 is/was something else, possibly the
lack of _negotiation_ of packet size.  Talking to Verl Boan (hope
I spelled that correctly), the CIXCD's were designed to be able
to handle 4K packets, but the firmware never actually implemented
them.  When the CIPCA-AA and HSJ50's appeared on the scene, HSJ40's,
CIBCA's (is that the right designation for the BI adapter?) and
CIXCD's, as well as HSC70's and 90's, only did 512 byte packets.
IIRC, the CIPCA's and HSJ50's negotiated packet size with the
"other end". For the first few years, only CIPCA <--> HSJ50 could
do 4K packets.  About 2 years ago, possibly earlier, new firmware
was released (finally) so that the CIXCD's could also do 4K packets.
In any case, my guess is that (very much) older hardware/firmware
could not do the negotiation and that's why the HSC50 had to be
removed from the CI.  If you look at the SPD for CIPCA and/or HSJ50,
there were only the CIBCA of a certain recent enough -xy, and the
CIXCD that could be on the same CI as the CIPCA and HSJ50.  I last
looked at this about 5 years ago so the specifics have long since
left volatile memory...but I do know what we had on the CI when
I added our first HSJ50s and AS4100 w/CIPCA...

    -Ken
