tonytee wrote:

> 3 NI   19210770 ?


The maintenance manual states that the
codes should look like 00000xxx,
but it then goes on to show examples
that don't fit the pattern (like
yours!).

Assuming your error code is
really 770, the manual claims that
the problem is in the I/O cover
or the external connection.

To check insert both an AUI
loopback and a BNC T piece with
two terminators (i.e. the shortest
possible thinwire ethernet).

Repeat the tests with the selector
switch in each position. If it works
on one but not the other, then one
of you ethernet driver chips in the cover
(at least I think that's where they are)
is dead. The easiest fix is to use the
other style of connector!

My guess is that either you had the switch

set the wrong way, or whichever of the two
styles (BNC or AUI) you are trying to use
is broken (off card, probably, and on the
I/O panel itself).



Antonio

