Your RD53 is probably suffering from the "sticky parked" condition. The
cushion the head actuator arm rests against decays and becomes tacky.
The drive tries to spin up but the arm can't move so the positioner
servo over currents and shuts down.

You'll need to find another RD53 (micropolis 1325 or 1335) or an RD54.

Jeff Campbell
n8wxs@arrl.net

