Hi John and Rick.  Thanks for your replies.

It's like Xmas at my place.  I was able to get my hands on a 900TM,
which allowed me to do some playing with the REMOTE PASSWORD
capabilities on it.

John - I have to agree with you about your uptime comment.  

From what I've seen after playing on the 900TM is that there is
something not quite right with the software on my 90M.  I can perform
the same sequence of commands on the 900TM and it will set the
password to what I tell it to.  Are you sure that it was the REMOTE
PASSWORD that you changed, and not one of the others (i.e. LOGIN or
PRIVILEGED)?  The software on my 90M is different from your customer's
unit, so it may be something with this particular version.

Rick - You should be able to set up your unit so that telnet
connections to port 20 are prompted ("#") for a password.  Here's the
sequence of steps that worked for me:

CHANGE SERVER REMOTE PASSWORD &#8220;password&#8221;	(default is
ACCESS)
CHANGE PORT nn ACCESS REMOTE
CHANGE TELNET LISTENER 20nn PORTS nn ENABLE
CHANGE TELNET LISTENER 20nn CONNECTIONS ENABLE
CHANGE PORT nn REMOTE PASSWORD ENABLE
LOGOUT PORT nn

The next time you connect to port nn, you should be prompted ("#") for
the REMOTE PASSWORD.  This should be whatever you typed in for
"password"...unless you are using my 90M, and then it would be ACCESS
:)

Joel


