> 
> Sounds like it's just a software issue, especially since it does work with
> the HSC70.  Doesn't the HSC70  uses the same CI interface module (L0100)
> as the HSC50?
> 
> Anyhow, I won't be connecting an HSC50 to the CIPCA.  The CIPCA will be
> connected to a CI20 on a KL10, and I want to write Linux software
> (including a CIPCA driver) to simulate an HSC50 in 576-byte-block mode
> for use with TOPS-10.

I think you are hosed.  IIRC, the CIPCA (both -AA and -BA versions)
can only share a CI with other nodes that support 4K packets; that's
why HSC50s and older CI host adapters are disallowed.  {ISTR that some
HSC70s and/or some CIXCDs/CIBCAs had to be brought up to rev for 4K
packets, but I won't swear to that.}  The CIPCA was never tried with
a CI20, and I'll give good odds that CI20s don't use 4K packets.
-- 
