Eric,

AlphaStations like yours need "True Parity" memory. I purchased memory for
my AlphaStation 200 4/100 from Kahlon www.kahlon.com for about $72 per 128
meg kit (2x64mb modules). I had no problem with the vendor and the memory
works fine in my system. I do NOT claim to be an authority on
AlphaStations - most of my experience is with VAXen. Your mileage may vary
:)

According to Kahlon's web page for your model, 512 mb is the system max. The
base memory is either 32 or 64 mb. A 128 mb kit (4x32mb) is DEC part number
MSP01-BC, Kahlon part number KAH1289, and as of THIS MINUTE, is priced at
$59. Kahlon shows the memory configured as 2 banks of 4 chips. I am not 100%
sure about this; my system uses memory 2 chips per bank. Anyone have any
comments?

I hope this helps. If someone else has better info, please jump in here!

Regards,
Stuart

