Apropos to the rather flash-burned photo of an alleged Marvel management
console on Mike Magee's site at www.theinquirer.net, I took the liberty of
stripping out about 10 Marvel-centric slides from the Compaq's Strategic
Directions for Enterprise-Centric Systems presentation I'll be doing in Lyon
next month at the ITUG/DECUS Joint Conference. The slides, which include
photos of 2P and 8P Marvel building blocks, a 64P Marvel system, and some
timeline information, are viewable at http://www.openvms.org and
http://www.tru64.org.

The photos themselves appear to have been taken at Compaq's "Marvel Mansion"
lab in Marlboro, MA. They reflect significant progress on the
next-generation enterprise server as there were no 64P (and not even any
32P) systems in evidence when I visited the Mansion late last year.

Enjoy,

terry s

