Bob Willard <BobwBSGS@attbi.com> writes:
> I don't think the CI780 could support 4K packets; that's why the CIPCA
> could not cohabitate with any CI780/CI750/CIBCI or HSC50 nodes.  And,
> I'll bet that the CI20 had the same restriction.

Paul Repacholi <prep@prep.synonet.com> writes:
> As the CI780/750 and the CI20 are the same HW, modulo the paddle boards,
> your money is pretty safe...

The "smarts" of the CI20 are on the IPA, which plugs into the KL10
Ebus and Cbus, modules M3001, M3002, and M3003.  These are definitely not
the same as any modules used on the CI780, since the latter is an SBI
device.  SBI is not even similar to the KL10 Ebus and Cbus.

I'm still hoping to find print sets, maintenance manuals, and other
docs on the HSC50, CI780, and CI750.  If I could get copies or borrow
them, scans would show up at http://www.spies.com/~aek/pdf/dec/


