> My system has 2 nic's. One onboard with both TenBT and Thick Ethernet and
> one extra one but I don't see that second one when I do a "show device" on
> the console. I only see the first one. I can set that first one from thick
> to tenbt and the other way around. I can do a "boot esa0" and then I see
> that he is trying to do a netboot of some kind but I only see IPX traffic.
> 
> Can anyone help me to find a way out of this problem?

The DEC 3000-400 boots fine over the network, but...

AFAIK, the only boot protocol it can use is MOP (and not IPX, what you 
think you have seen). It can boot from an other Alpha or VAX running 
OpenVMS to form a cluster. It does not try bootp.

The extra network card you have is a Turbochannel option. The console 
subsystem can only see that that there is something, but not what it is. 
You see a TC0 (Probably your video adapter) and a TC1 (your extra 
network card). My 3000-400 has two dual channel SCSI adapters (TC1 and 
TC2) but the console can't see any devices on those busses.

HTH (a little)

Bart Zorn





