:I'm trying to make a Dec3000/400 do a netboot but the only trafic from the
:MacAddress of this system I see on my network is IPX traffic. No BootP
:requests or anything for that matter.

  You'll need to acquire and configure a MOP server -- OpenVMS,
  Tru64 UNIX, ULTRIX, and various other platforms have this.
  One vendor had MOP running on SunOS some years ago.  It would
  not surprise me to see it running on Linux and other platforms.

  Newer firmware releases can use bootp and MOP.  If you want to
  perform a bootp bootstrap, specify the target boot device as EZ.
  If you specify the ES device, you get MOP.

  If you want to look into MOP, the DECnet Phase IV specifications 
  are referenced in the OpenVMS FAQ, and MOP itself is covered in 
  the DECnet maintenance and operations manual.

  What operating system are you seeking to download? 

  If this is hobbyist use, licenses for OpenVMS are available
  and details are in the FAQ.  Tru64 UNIX also has a similar
  hobbyist program, but the TURBOchannel boxes such as this 
  one are no longer supported by current releases.

