You are looking in the right place. The cable that plugs into that plug
on the front of the controller drops under the floor and connects to the
four CI cables.  The eliminates the necessity of getting four thick, stiff
cables (or thin, potentially fragile cables) threaded up into the cabinet
and through a VERY TIGHT (i.e., will break the cable) bend to come off the
front of the controller.

I have a few lying around since we converted to fiber. (also one pair
of HSJ40s). I can look up the cable number if you need it.  Presumably
the people who deinstalled the system have the cables -- or threw them
out or destroyed them.


