Actually I only want to make the PC act as an HSC50 in 576-byte-block
mode for use with the DECSYSTEM-10 under TOPS-10.  For that, most of the
stuff used to support distributed lock management and other VMS
clustering features will not be necessary.

I've got the source code for the TOPS-10 side of things, so I mostly
know what I need to implement.  TOPS-10 only uses the CI to read and write
disk blocks (and tape) on an HSC50; it doesn't use any fancy stuff.   The
CIPCA interface is the only part about which I have insufficient information.

If all else fails, it looks like it would only take a few months of
spare time to design a new FPGA-based PCI CI interface card.  Most of
the logic other than the PCI interface can be similar to what's in the
CI20.  But since I already have the CIPCA in hand, I'd rather not waste
time reinventing that wheel.


