Here is the definitive explanation

Green - initial color for WIde and Narrow
Gray - OEM color for Storageworks drives - both Wide and Narrow
Used by Siemens Nixdorf, IDL Netframe etc.
Blue - Compaq's new server color for both Wide and Narrow
White - for DEC's Prioris and Alpha NT boxes - only Wide AFAIK


The blue and White  were all Ultra XXX, - the others were older style

As for the cables, once SCA (80 pin) came out, Compaq set this as their
standard for
both UW and Narrow disks
They did this by using the 17-04028-02 as their wide-wide cable and the
17-04028-07 as the Wide to Narrow cable

Ergo they could use generic and easy to supply disks that were functionally
wide and make them into 8 bit narrow disks

Smart if you ask me..

