If you're logged in as SYSTEM, you should have two symbols:

$ show symbol shutdown
  SHUTDOWN == "@SYS$SYSTEM:SHUTDOWN 0 SHUTDOWN YES NO LATER NO NONE"
$ show symbol reboot
  REBOOT == "@SYS$SYSTEM:SHUTDOWN 0 SHUTDOWN YES NO LATER YES NONE"

Just enter either SHUTDOWN or REBOOT at the DCL prompt - just like UN*X,
sort of. In UN*X-land, it's actually "halt" rather than shutdown, AFAIK.
