Jan-Erik S�derholm wrote:

>There is no real reason to use diff-SCSI if you
>don't need to use a SCSI bus up to 25 meters. Otherwise
>it's a waste. I tought that it was mainly the external
>HSZ40/50/70/80 controllers that used diff-SCSI. Never heard
>of any StorageWorks disk that had that built in.
