Yes, for its day.

You snipped out something important ...

>> Nothing necessarily prevents one from building a Lisp/Pascal/Ada ...
>> microprocessor.  But for it to be commercially successful, it would have to
>> (1) compete cycle for cycle with other general-purpose micros and (2)
