provide the additional microcode etc. to support formatting disks.  This
was several years before LSI floppy controller chips were available.  It
would have taken more PROMs for microcode storage and more SSI/MSI chips
for the other necessary support.

Other vendors (notably DSD) did seize the opportunity to offer compatible
floppy disk subsystems that supported formatting.




