A few examples of some popular uses of Lisp:

 Scheduling Systems (such as airlines, space shuttle)
 Military Planning
 Communication Networks - Design, Analysis, Monitoring
 Real-Time Process Control (such factory automation)
 Telephone Switching
 Billing Systems
 CAD Design (structural engineering, PC boards, chips)
 Computer Algebra for all kinds of science & engineering ("egg head stuff"?)
 Medical and Bioinformatics
 Hypertext Documentation
 Text Editors
 Web Servers
 Data Mining
 Artificial Intelligence (robots, natural language understanding, etc.)
 Space Flight (eg. on board the Mars Pathfinder probe)
 Financial Analysis (P&L scenarios)
 Graphics and Animation (TV/Cable/Movies, Theme Park Rides, etc.)

You can find some more information about this at places like
 <http://www.lisp.org/table/commercial-use.htm>

Why are these not "real world" computing?
What application areas were you thinking of?


