> the RX50 drive itself.
> 
In one project we had a microvax-ii that we had to backup on floppies.
We found that about 5 foppies of 100 could not be written. First we
thought that these was defective, but later we found that if you 
removed and then inserted the floppy again, it was ok. 

Thus the problem was that the floppy was not always centered on the
hub in the RX50. Since a saveset was some 80-100 floppies, if we
had format/backup/verified in one go, the probability that we ever could
restore the set again was very low.

Soloution to the problem... don't fix the floppy drives, sell
preformated floppies instead.

/Thord.




