While I lay no claim to the definitive definition here, my impression is
that part of the difference involves behavior under load.  I remember not so
fondly the way RSX-11M systems (back around V2 - V3?  1976ish, anyway) would
clutch up and die under excessive user load ('pool' - I think primary -
exhaustion being one memorable problem which occasionally could be unwound
by judicious task removal but as often could not), whereas I'd expect a real
time-sharing system just to get slower and slower but keep chugging away.

