First I assume since you don't say that you have Tru64 (DIGITAL Unix,OSF1)
on the machine. If not then tell us what you do have...
I also assume you have physical access to the machine

Start with the machine switched off and yourself at the console.

1 power on the machine...
2 If it boots to the console prompt '>>>' then go to step 4
3 If it doesn't pres ^C repeatedly as early in the boot process
as you can, it should stop at the prompt(You can also use the halt
button if the machine has one).
4 At the >>> prompt type boot -fl s
5 The system should boot to single user mode.
6 use bcheckrc to mount and enable access to the disks
7 change the root password using passwd.
8 reboot your machine.
HTH
Adam





