Another datapoint from memory : 

At my college the DEC2065 tended to get slow at round 150 users, where
around 100 would be active at any one time. It only got terminally
bad at two occations; both under severe stress from a lot of different
work.

At my first job we observed VAX780's not be able to run a simple
videotext application for more than around 20 users without massive
overloading. It was swapping and taskswitching itself to death.
It was not until the 8600 that there was a real platform for VMS
that could take any major loads. 

The same application flew on both Prime 750's and Nord 100's; both
with slower cpus and less memory. I never got a chance to test it
on a '20. (although, now with emulators I may get a chance. I still 
have the source code). 

This was around 1985. 

