Just to add. I think a typical syntax for booting a linux install CD would be:

Get it down to 1 hard disk and 1 CDrom and try:

>>> boot dka600 -file vmlinux.gz -flags "root=sdb2"

"Vmlinux.gz" or whatever the kernel name is, is usually on boot partiton 1 by
default. 

b would be the scsi "b" drive = CD and usually root is on partition 2.

