Anthony:

Boot server, determine if SRM or AlphaBios is running.  If screen
displays:
>>>_
Then you are in SRM console
Type:
>>>set os_type NT
-or, if that doesn't work-
>>>arc

Then powercycle the computer.
AlphaBios *should* now display.
Insert NT4 CDRom.
There *might* be an option in your version of AlphaBios which will allow
you to "Install NT from CDRom", if it's there, then use it to install
NT.
If it's not there, there *should* be a feature somewhere in the
supplementary menus that allows you to run a program, select this option
and type:
cdrom\alpha\arcinst.exe

Good luck!

TomC



