ok. I can only say here that this is how we booted a RED HAT linux install cd
with one scsi hard disk and one scsi cd:

>>> boot dka*00 -fi "kernels/generic.gz" -fl "root=/dev/sdb"

We also had IDE drive and IDE CDrom which would be:
>>> boot dqa1 -fi "kernels/generic.gz" -fl "root=/dev/hdb"

dqa1 is the (srm) IDE cdrom; hdb is the (linux) cdrom path.

hope this helps..
Bob



