Hi all,

Do any of you know how to determine whether a NIC is full duplex or half
duplex under Tru64? Under FreeBSD, this information can be retrieve by
using "ifconfig".

tl0: flags=8843<UP,BROADCAST,RUNNING,SIMPLEX,MULTICAST> mtu 1500
        ether 00:50:8b:dc:8a:75
        media: Ethernet 100baseTX <full-duplex>
        status: active

Note that the "media" line tells you this card if full duplex.

There is a SIOCIFSETCHAR (struct ifchar) under ioctl, but there doesn't
seem to be any read interface. Has anyone bumped into this before?

Andrew



